  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper compares three gate-based QML models for credit card fraud detection on two datasets: VQC, SQNN, and EQNN. On BankSim, the best reported FI-scores are 0.71 for VQC, 0.85 for SQNN, and 0.59 for EQNN; on the European dataset, the best reported FI-scores are 0.88 for VQC, 0.84 for SQNN, and 0.52 for EQNN. All experiments are simulator-based using Qiskit Aer/QasmSimulator, with 4-6 qubits and 350 maximum iterations, and no practical quantum advantage over classical baselines is demonstrated.",
